      'Fix: Live FE crashes never made it into the #patchman-support Slack channel even with the React-render-crashes toggle on AND the webhook configured AND the admin Test integration button delivering successfully. handlers/error_report.go Report() launched the Slack POST in a goroutine that captured `c.Request.Context()` — but Gin/net-http cancels the request context the instant the handler returns and the 204 lands on the wire. The goroutine\'s `http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, …)` then fired with an already-cancelled context, `client.Do` returned `context.Canceled` immediately, and the payload was silently dropped. Test integration kept working because PostRaw runs synchronously inside the handler — the request context is still alive when client.Do completes. The async path was the only broken one, which is exactly the path real crashes go through.',
